WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.469
Better learning design begins with performance.

2
00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:09.464
What should learners be able to do after the course that they could not do reliably before?

3
00:00:09.464 --> 00:00:17.282
Once that outcome is clear, the objective, examples, practice, feedback, and assessment can all point in the same direction.

4
00:00:17.282 --> 00:00:21.808
If the goal is decision quality, the course should include decisions.

5
00:00:21.808 --> 00:00:26.746
If the goal is procedure accuracy, the course should include procedural practice.

6
00:00:26.746 --> 00:00:32.095
If the goal is judgment, the course should expose learners to realistic tradeoffs.

7
00:00:32.095 --> 00:00:32.918
Sequencing matters.

8
00:00:32.918 --> 00:00:41.148
Learners often benefit from concrete examples before abstract rules, simple cases before complex ones, and guided practice before independent performance.

9
00:00:41.148 --> 00:00:47.320
Summaries and reflection help learners consolidate what they noticed and connect it to future use.

10
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:52.257
Feedback loops help them improve while there is still time to adjust.

11
00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:58.841
Assessment alignment keeps the course honest by measuring the capability the instruction was supposed to build.

12
00:00:58.841 --> 00:01:01.310
Good design also avoids information dumps.

13
00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:04.190
More content is not automatically more learning.

14
00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:09.128
A course can be comprehensive and still be structured, focused, and usable.

15
00:01:09.128 --> 00:01:17.357
Inclusive and accessible design strengthens learning by reducing unnecessary barriers and making participation more reliable across different learners and environments.

16
00:01:17.357 --> 00:01:19.826
The aim is not passive completion.

17
00:01:19.826 --> 00:01:25.998
The aim is to create conditions where people can build durable understanding and usable skill.

18
00:01:25.998 --> 00:01:29.702
This does not require every course to be elaborate.

19
00:01:29.702 --> 00:01:42.869
Even a short module can be stronger when it states a performance goal, uses a concrete example, asks learners to retrieve or apply the idea, and gives feedback that points to improvement.

20
00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:51.098
The discipline is to spend course time on the things most likely to change what the learner can do afterward.
